1
00:00:05,622 --> 00:00:13,871
Now let’s machine the sign. Operations live on the Machining tab, on the right.

2
00:00:13,871 --> 00:00:18,942
First the cut-out. With nothing selected, Profile takes the part outline.

3
00:00:18,942 --> 00:00:22,021
The tool is picked automatically: T101, the 12 mm cut-out cutter. The blue line is its path.

4
00:00:22,021 --> 00:00:25,809
Amber notes list placeholder values still to confirm, like feeds and speeds. Configure opens each one.

5
00:00:25,809 --> 00:00:28,782
Happy with it? Accept toolpath.

6
00:00:28,782 --> 00:00:37,198
Next the recess. Select the panel rectangle, then Add operation, Pocket.

7
00:00:37,198 --> 00:00:45,624
The pocket clears everything inside, ring by ring. Set the depth to 1/8".

8
00:00:45,624 --> 00:00:53,394
Last the hanging holes. With nothing selected, Drill takes all the holes.

9
00:00:53,394 --> 00:00:57,524
The holes are 5/16" (7.94 mm). That is within the drill tolerance of the 8 mm dowel drill, so T203 is picked by itself.

10
00:00:57,524 --> 00:01:03,617
Switch on Cut through so the holes go right through the board.

11
00:01:03,617 --> 00:01:09,037
New operations go in before the cut-out, so the part is still held while it is pocketed and drilled. The cut-out stays last.
